{#
  T-4.04 — the heading that opens a home section.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.ui.section-header' with {
        title: section.title,
        url:   section.display_all_url,
        level: 2
    } %}

  Parameters:
    title   required — the section's own title setting. Never a literal.
    level   1–6, default 2. See WHY LEVEL IS A PARAMETER below.
    url     optional — when present, the «عرض الكل» action is rendered.
    align   'center' (default) or 'start'.
    id      optional — set it when a section wants aria-labelledby on itself.

  WHY LEVEL IS A PARAMETER. A heading's level is a statement about the document
  it lands in, not about how it looks. The same section can sit under an <h1> on
  Home and under an <h2> inside a page that already has its own heading, and a
  component that hard-codes <h2> makes the outline wrong in one of those two
  places. Size is a class here; level is an argument. They are not the same
  decision and this partial refuses to conflate them.

  WHY TWO ALIGNMENTS. Both appear in `Home Page (No Scroll).pdf` and neither is
  a mistake: «Winter Is Coming» is centred with the action centred beneath it,
  and «تجارب عملائنا» is start-aligned with no action at all. Centre is the
  default because that is the arrangement this task's objective describes.

  WHY THE LINK SAYS MORE THAN IT SHOWS. «عرض الكل» repeated down a page gives a
  screen-reader user a list of identical links to nowhere in particular — WCAG
  2.4.4 is about exactly this. The section title is appended in visually-hidden
  text, so the accessible name becomes «عرض الكل Winter Is Coming» while the
  visible label stays as drawn. Appending rather than replacing is deliberate:
  2.5.3 asks that the accessible name CONTAIN the visible label, so a voice-input
  user saying "عرض الكل" still matches.

  The visible label is upstream's own `blocks.home.display_all`, not a new theme
  key — the string already exists in every locale Salla ships.
#}
{% set section_header_level = level|default(2) %}
{% set section_header_align = align|default('center') %}

<div class="section-header section-header--{{ section_header_align }}">
    <h{{ section_header_level }} class="section-header__title"
        {% if id is defined and id is not empty %}id="{{ id }}"{% endif %}>{{ title }}</h{{ section_header_level }}>

    {% if url is defined and url is not empty %}
        <a class="section-header__action" href="{{ url }}">
            {{ trans('blocks.home.display_all') }}<span class="sr-only"> {{ title }}</span>
        </a>
    {% endif %}
</div>
